findings.recommendation:
Three cheap changes, none touching shared code:
1. Correct the [020] note in docs/tech-debt.md instead of extending it: the class was already reachable on every diffed screen because `Ncols` is archive-controlled and `validate()` does not check it against `len(Cols)`. Record the actually-new shape (same PG version, differing width from a pgcenter-version boundary under `record -a`) and why it is currently benign.
2. Add the missing sentence to Decision 1: tail placement keeps `DiffIntvl[1]` inside the narrower layout's row width, which is what makes the mixed-width same-version pair safe. State that the margin is zero on both screens.
3. Turn it into a test in Task 2, next to the `DiffIntvl[1] == Ncols-2` assertion the spec already plans:

```go
// The diff interval is inclusive, so DiffIntvl[1] is the highest index diff()
// hands to prev.Values[j]. A same-PG-version archive can pair a narrow sample
// with a wide one (record -a across a pgcenter upgrade), and report.go's
// versionChanged branch does not catch it. Keep the upper bound inside the
// NARROWEST layout or that pair panics.
for _, v := range []int{query.PostgresV14, query.PostgresV19} {
    _, ncols, intvl := query.SelectStatTablesQuery(v)
    require.Less(t, intvl[1], minNcolsAcrossVersions, "DiffIntvl[1]=%d escapes the narrowest layout", intvl[1])
    _ = ncols
}
```
where `minNcolsAcrossVersions` is the minimum `Ncols` the selector returns over the supported version list. Same for `SelectStatIndexesQuery`.

Add a `SetupTestRole` pair to Task 1's integration test, mirroring `archiver_test.go:212-250`:

```go
// The claim "the new view needs no special privileges" was measured by hand as
// superuser. Every test connection is superuser too, so nothing re-measures it.
// Pin both role shapes: a GA that restricts the view changes no column name and
// would otherwise redden nothing.
for _, tc := range []struct{ role string; monitor bool }{
    {avScoresRoleMonitor, true},
    {avScoresRoleNoRole, false},
} {
    require.NoError(t, postgres.SetupTestRole(conn, tc.role, tc.monitor))
    rows, err := conn.Conn.Query(context.Background(), q)
    require.NoError(t, err, "role %s cannot read pg_stat_autovacuum_scores", tc.role)
    rows.Close()
}
```
Use a role name unique to this test file — internal/stat/postgres_test.go:241 records that `SetupTestRole`'s DO block is not atomic and two packages sharing a role name race. Also soften the Risks row: state that the locked column-name test covers renames and set changes, not ACL changes, and that the role test is what covers the latter.

Optional, one line in Task 2's test, where the layout assertions already live:

```go
// ViewType is spliced into a relation name in five query constants. Its domain
// is enforced only by the two literals in toggleSysTables; pin it here so a
// future third value fails a test instead of a query.
for _, vt := range []string{"user", "all"} {
    q, err := query.Format(query.PgStatTablesPG19, query.Options{ViewType: vt})
    require.NoError(t, err)
    require.Contains(t, q, "pg_stat_"+vt+"_tables")
}
```
No change to the new query is warranted — its `{{if ne}}` form is the right one and should be the pattern for future screens.
